{number: 166}
{title: Pass It On}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
It [C] only takes a spark to [Em] get a fire going,
And [F] soon all those a-[G7] round can warm up in its glowing;
[C] That's how it is with God's [Em] love,
Once you've ex-[F] perienced [C] it,
You [F] spread His love to [C] everyone,
You [Dm] want to [G7] pass it [C] on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
What a [C] wondrous time is spring, when [Em] all the trees are budding,
The [F] birds begin to sing, the [G7] flowers start their blooming;
[C] That's how it is with God's [Em] love,
Once you've ex-[F] perienced [C] it,
You [F] want to sing, it's [C] fresh like spring,
You [Dm] want to [G7] pass it [C] on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I [C] wish for you, my friend, this [Em] happiness that I've found;
You [F] can depend on Him, it [G7] matters not where you're bound;
[C] I'll shout it from the [Em] mountaintop,
I [F] want my world to [C] know:
The [F] Lord of love has [C] come to me,
I [Dm] want to [G7] pass it [C] on.
{end_of_verse}
